DOCKER BASIC COMMANDS:

Image: A read-only template/package containing the application code, dependencies, libraries, runtime, and configuration needed to run an application.
Container: A running (or stopped) isolated instance of a Docker image, where the application executes.
docker run image: To run the entire application
SETUP:
-> Download docker for desktop
-> Set up in the IDE using extension
-> Set up the code structure
-> Create the "dockerfile" and start the server by "npm install" and "npm run dev" 
-> Commands:
#Uses node version 22 as our base image
FROM node:22
#Goes to app directory
WORKDIR /app
#Copy package.json and package-lock.json
copy package*.json ./
#Install app dependencies
RUN npm install
#Copy the rest of the app into the container
COPY . .
#Set port environment variable
ENV PORT=3000
EXPOSE 3000
#Run the app
CMD ["npm","start"]
-> Now, in the terminal docker built -t dockerimagename "-t-> tag name for image"
-> Then, run the container by , docker run -p 3000:3000 containername -p->port forwarding and 3000->computer port; 3000->container port
-> docker scout quickfile->analysis of dependencies and vulnerabilities if any and how to handle them 
Multi-Container application:
-> Having frontend, backend and database separately as containers
-> There is necessity to run all these containers separately, so we use DOCKER COMPOSE[to connect all containers and run the full application]
-> Create compose.yaml
-> services:
  frontend:
    build: ./frontend
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    depends_on:
      - backend

  backend:
    build: ./backend
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"
    depends_on:
      - db

  db:
    image: postgres:16
    environment:
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password
-> Docker Volume: is used to persist data even after containers are stopped or removed and share data between containers.
services:
  frontend:
    build: ./frontend
    ports:
      - "3000:3000"
    depends_on:
      - backend

  backend:
    build: ./backend
    ports:
      - "5000:5000"
    depends_on:
      - db

  db:
    image: postgres:16
    environment:
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password
# Start all containers
docker compose up -d

# Stop all containers
docker compose down
